# Copyright (c) d-SEAMS developers
# Build every VMD molfile plugin that returns atoms and that this tree can
# compile, and register each reader as a chemfiles format. With the three
# default plugins (gromacs, molden, psf) that is 33 plugins and 37 molfile
# formats. gromacsplugin also registers its g96 reader; chemfiles has no
# G96 reader of its own. dmsplugin links the system SQLite3. cpmdlogplugin
# and gaussianplugin compile once molfile_plugin.h has the QM fields they
# write. That header edit, and the fixes for hostile files, are applied to
# molfiles.tar.gz by chemfiles-0.10.4-external-sources.sh.
#
# Left unbuilt, each for a reason recorded in
# docs/orgmode/reference/data-formats.org: cifplugin (no source), crdplugin
# and vtfplugin's vcf reader (no atom count without a topology), babelplugin
# (runs an external babel), basissetplugin (no atoms), hoomdplugin (needs
# expat.h, which the frozen env does not ship), webpdbplugin (Tcl and a
# network fetch), the plugins chemfiles already implements itself, and the
# graphics and volumetric plugins, which Molfile<F> cannot read atoms from.
#
# Molfile<F> also changes for these plugins: nsteps() counts into scratch
# buffers instead of a null timestep (rst7 crashed on a valid file), an
# empty file is an error before a plugin sees it (rst7 crashed on one),
# an AMBER7 restart without an atom count on its second line is an error
# (rst7 looped forever on one), and a plugin that reports no atoms is an
# error instead of a std::vector length error. A frame read first asks
# for the timestep and QM timestep metadata, since the QM log plugins
# parse the next frame there, and passes no QM timestep, which the
# patched plugins take as "coordinates only" (GAMESS and CPMD logs wrote
# through null). Fixed-width plugin fields are read up to their size, a
# bond list that is null or names atom 0 is an error, nsteps() is an
# error when the plugin cannot re-open the file or then reports another
# atom count (vtfplugin read through a null handle), S_ISREG is defined
# where the C library lacks it (MSVC), and the Molfile constructor uses an
# RAII guard so the plugin handle is closed and finalized if any step
# (including read_topology) throws.
# A file named clickme.dtr is the DESRES trajectory the plugin opens.
# It is not rejected by the empty-file probe or by the atom-count
# versus file-size check. Every other empty file, including an empty
# .dtr that is not named clickme.dtr, still is.
